('chapter-23','chapter','Introverts and Extroverts','Introverts and Extroverts - Main Presentation',0,'https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/greentea/chapter/introverts-and-extroverts-main-presentation/','[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Watch this lecture and take notes."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"You can review the questions before you watch the video, and answer them after you watch:"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"1. What are the main ideas in this presentation? 2. What is the correct definition of introverts? Give examples and details from the video. 3. What is the correct definition of extroverts? Give examples and details from the video. 4. What is the meaning of \"ambiverts\"? 5. How can this information help you? 6. Do you consider yourself an introvert or an extrovert? Why? Explain your answer with some examples from your life."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Click here if you want to open the video in another tab and watch it full screen."}]'::jsonb,112),
('chapter-52','chapter','Introverts and Extroverts','Vocabulary 1 - Introverts and Extroverts',1,'https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/greentea/chapter/vocabulary-1-introverts-and-extroverts/','[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Read and focus on the bold words in these examples."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Have you seen them before? Are they new?"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Take notes about the meaning, translation, and/or part of speech."}]'::jsonb,28),
('chapter-54','chapter','Introverts and Extroverts','Vocabulary 2 - Introverts and Extroverts',2,'https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/greentea/chapter/vocabulary-2-introverts-and-extroverts/','[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Read and focus on the bold words."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Have you seen them before? Are they new?"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Take notes about the meaning, translation, and/or part of speech."}]'::jsonb,25),
('chapter-47','chapter','Introverts and Extroverts','Strengths and Weaknesses of Extroverts',3,'https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/greentea/chapter/strengths-and-weaknesses-of-extroverts/','[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Watch the video and take notes. Can you catch all the main ideas?"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"There are 5-6 strengths of extroverts, and 5 weaknesses."}]'::jsonb,22),
('chapter-49','chapter','Introverts and Extroverts','Pronunciation Practice A - Introverts and Extroverts',4,'https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/greentea/chapter/pronunciation-practice-introverts-and-extroverts/','[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Practice saying the reading out loud slowly, loudly, and clearly. You can record your voice and listen to it below."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"After you practice , use a phone or computer to record yourself reading out loud, and send the recording to your teacher."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Now I’m familiar with the terms extroverts and introverts. Some people think introverts are individuals who are very shy and aren’t social. This is a misconception! Introverts are individuals who need some time alone to recharge their energy. They like to be around people, and it’s fun to hang out with them, but sometimes they prefer to be alone. This may be difficult for an extrovert to understand."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Everyone has different pronunciation challenges. Which ones are important for you?"}]'::jsonb,121),
('chapter-213','chapter','Introverts and Extroverts','Pronunciation Practice B - Past Tense, Introverts and Extroverts',5,'https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/greentea/chapter/pronunciation-practice-b-past-tense-introverts-and-extroverts/','[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Practice saying the reading out loud slowly, loudly, and clearly. You can record your voice and listen to it below."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"After you practice , use a phone or computer to record yourself reading out loud, and send the recording to your teacher."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Before, Eric thought that introverts were shy people. But when he heard information, read, thought, and spoke about the topic, he understood more. Now he knew that this was a misconception! He saw that introverts were individuals who need some time alone to recharge their energy. Because of the practice that we did, he found a new way to understand both introverts and extroverts."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Can you find the past tense verbs? There are 13 of them."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Also, everyone has different pronunciation challenges. Which ones are important for you?"}]'::jsonb,130),
('chapter-215','chapter','Introverts and Extroverts','Finishing the notes from the lecture (interactive activity)',6,'https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/greentea/chapter/finishing-the-notes-from-the-lecture-interactive-activity/','[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Drag and drop the words in each part to finish the notes from the lecture. Notice the organization of main ideas and details."}]'::jsonb,23),
