('chapter-335','chapter','Language, Memory, and Aphasia','Content and Function Words - about Aphasia',20,'https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/greentea/chapter/content-and-function-words-about-aphasia/','[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Read, focus, and record"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"We have practiced finding stressed content words and reduced function words. Can you find the stressed content words below? Read them out loud, and try to stress the content words, and reduce the function words."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"You can also listen and repeat with Eric in the video below."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"You can practice with this recording button:"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Watch, listen, and repeat. Can you hear the stressed content words? Can you see them? Remember, stress is usually \"big\" — you can see bigger mouth movements and maybe even eye or eyebrow movements, too."}]'::jsonb,93),
